"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[4951],{4951:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"id":"base-g1","slug":"base-g1","trackId":"base","order":14,"title":"OKX Wallet: A Step-by-Step Guide","subtitle":"Clear Rules for Protecting Capital","estimatedMinutes":8,"access":"free","quizCount":3,"blueprintCount":0,"trainerIds":["HUB-CALC-04"],"markdown":"Guide 1 \xb7 8 steps \xb7 6 min\\n\\n## OKX Wallet\\n\\nCreating and configuring OKX Wallet\\n\\nIn this guide, we will create a first cryptocurrency wallet, configure its security and explore its main functions.\\n\\nYou do not need to memorize everything immediately. This practical guide is something you can return to whenever you need to create a new wallet, remember how to receive cryptocurrency, configure security or recover access.\\n\\nSome terms and features may still be unfamiliar. That is normal — we will gradually explain how everything works throughout the course. Our example uses OKX Wallet ↗ (opens in a new tab), a non-custodial cryptocurrency wallet supporting many blockchain networks. Non-custodial means you control access to the funds yourself, rather than an exchange or another company.\\n\\nOKX Wallet is available on smartphones and computers. This guide uses the Google Chrome browser extension. A browser wallet is convenient for learning about cryptocurrency and interacting with services. To store significant amounts, use a separate device (computer or phone) and a more secure storage arrangement. Completed – of 8.\\n- 1\\n\\n### Step 1: Installing OKX Wallet\\n\\nVisit the official website:\\n\\nhttps://web3.okx.com ↗ (opens in a new tab)\\n\\nFind the wallet download section and choose the Google Chrome extension. The website will redirect you to the Chrome Web Store, where you can install OKX Wallet. Click “Add to Chrome” and confirm the installation. A wallet icon will appear in the browser. If it is not visible, click the extensions icon at the top right of Chrome and pin OKX Wallet for quick access.\\n\\nImportant: install the wallet only through the official website and check the extension\'s developer. Fake extensions on the internet can look almost identical to the original.\\n- 2\\n\\n### Step 2: Creating a Wallet\\n\\nOpen the installed OKX Wallet extension. On the start screen, choose “Create Wallet.” If the app offers several creation methods, choose “Seed Phrase Wallet.” Do not choose “Import Wallet”: that function restores an existing wallet.\\n\\nNext, create a strong password for access to the extension. Prefer a unique password that you do not use for other services.\\n\\nImportant: the password protects access to the wallet on this computer, but it does not replace the seed phrase. Anyone who learns your seed phrase can restore the wallet on another device without knowing the password.\\n- 3\\n\\n### Step 3: Saving the Seed Phrase\\n\\nThis is the most important part of creating a wallet. OKX Wallet will ask you to save a seed phrase: a sequence of English words that restores access to cryptocurrency. It usually contains 12 words. You need the phrase if you lose the computer, delete the extension or want to restore the wallet on another device.\\n\\nAnyone who obtains your seed phrase could potentially steal every asset in the wallet.\\n\\nFollow these rules:\\n- Write the words on paper in the correct order.\\n- Do not take screenshots of the seed phrase.\\n- Do not save it in text files, notes or cloud storage.\\n- Do not send it to yourself through Telegram, WhatsApp or email.\\n- Do not show it to other people, even if they claim to be OKX support staff.\\n- Keep the written copy somewhere safe and inaccessible to others.\\n\\nAfter saving it, check that every word is correct and in the right order. If the wallet offers a seed phrase check, complete it. Never enter the seed phrase on third-party websites. It is not required to receive cryptocurrency, connect to DeFi or approve ordinary transactions.\\n- 4\\n\\n### Step 4: Exploring the Interface\\n\\nAfter creation, the OKX Wallet home screen opens. It shows the balance, a list of cryptocurrencies and the main functions. Receive means receiving cryptocurrency at your address. Send means transferring cryptocurrency to another wallet or exchange.\\n\\nSwap means exchanging one cryptocurrency for another. The wallet also lets you switch networks, view transaction history and connect to cryptocurrency services. Start by learning the main functions. There is no need to try every feature immediately.\\n- 5\\n\\n### Step 5: Finding the Wallet Address\\n\\nTo receive cryptocurrency, you need your wallet\'s address.\\n- Open OKX Wallet.\\n- Click “Receive.”\\n- Choose the cryptocurrency and network on which you intend to receive funds.\\n- Copy the address displayed by the wallet.\\n\\nAn address can be compared with a bank account number. You can share it with others so that they can send you cryptocurrency. But there is an important difference.\\n\\nIn cryptocurrency, you must consider both the address and the transfer network.\\n\\nFor example, USDT and USDC exist on multiple networks. When sending, make sure the sender\'s network matches the network on which you intend to receive the funds. Choosing the wrong network can cause a loss of funds. Before every transfer, carefully check the address, selected network and asset itself.\\n- 6\\n\\n### Step 6: Configuring Security\\n\\nAfter creating the wallet, check several things. Password: use a unique, sufficiently complex password for the extension. Automatic lock: enable wallet locking after a period of inactivity in security settings, if the installed version provides it. Seed phrase: make sure it is recorded correctly and stored separately from the computer.\\n\\nBrowser and operating system: install security updates regularly. Extensions: do not install unknown or suspicious browser extensions. Some can access website content and create additional risks.\\n\\nPrograms and files: do not run unknown applications or files from unverified sources. Malware on a computer can threaten cryptocurrency wallets. Website connections: do not connect a wallet to unknown services, and carefully check every operation before approving it.\\n\\nA browser wallet runs on a computer that may be used for many other tasks. We therefore do not recommend keeping significant amounts in a wallet installed on an everyday work computer. For substantial savings, use a separate device or a more secure storage arrangement.\\n- 7\\n\\n### Step 7: Testing the Wallet\\n\\nBefore transferring significant amounts, test the wallet with a small transfer.\\n- Open OKX Wallet and click “Receive.”\\n- Choose the required cryptocurrency and network.\\n- Copy the receiving address.\\n- Send a small amount from another wallet or exchange.\\n- Wait for transaction confirmation.\\n- Make sure the funds appear in the balance.\\n\\nIf necessary, try sending a small amount back. Remember that sending cryptocurrency usually requires a network fee. For example, fees on Ethereum ↗ (opens in a new tab) are paid in ETH. If you have USDT but no ETH to cover the fee on that network, you cannot send USDT in the ordinary way.\\n\\nBefore sending, always check whether you have the cryptocurrency required to pay the fee.\\n- 8\\n\\n### Step 8: What to Do if You Lose Wallet Access\\n\\nDeleting the extension, reinstalling the browser or losing the computer does not mean the cryptocurrency disappears. The funds are on the blockchain; OKX Wallet simply provides a way to manage them. To restore access:\\n- Install the official OKX Wallet on a trusted device.\\n- Choose “Import Wallet.”\\n- Choose recovery using a seed phrase.\\n- Enter the saved words in the correct order.\\n- Set a new password for access to the extension.\\n\\nAfter recovery, you can manage your funds again. But if the seed phrase is lost and you no longer have access to the wallet anywhere, recovering the funds is generally impossible. That is why correctly saving the seed phrase during wallet creation is so important.\\n\\n### Conclusion\\n\\nYou now have your own cryptocurrency wallet installed in the browser. You know how to:\\n- install the OKX Wallet extension;\\n- create a wallet;\\n- save the seed phrase;\\n- configure basic security settings;\\n- find an address for receiving cryptocurrency;\\n- test the wallet with a small transfer;\\n- restore access after losing the computer.\\n\\nThe main thing to remember: a cryptocurrency wallet lets you manage your funds yourself, but responsibility for their security is yours too. ← Lesson 12 Forecast Sellers \xb7 Directory → Services From the Course\\n\\n### Terms Used in This Lesson:\\n- **Blockchain** — A record of all transactions that everyone can inspect: entries can be added, but old entries cannot be changed. It is stored simultaneously on millions of computers, making falsification of the history physically impossible\\n- **DeFi (Decentralized Finance)** — An attempt to rebuild the banking system with smart contracts: no banks, offices or employees, only code. It operates 24/7, but without insurance. Both a revolution and a casino\\n- **Ethereum** — Not a currency but a platform, a “world computer,” running smart contracts, DeFi and most stablecoins. Second-largest in size and trust\\n- **USDC** — Circle’s stablecoin, considered the most transparent: regular audits and clearly described reserves\\n- **USDT (Tether)** — The largest stablecoin, supporting almost all crypto turnover. For Russians after 2022, a practical tool for cross-border transfers outside banks\\n- **Seed Phrase** — 12 or 24 words used to restore a wallet. Whoever has the phrase controls the money, so neither support staff nor project administrators need to ask for it\\n- **Non-Custodial Wallet** — A wallet where you, rather than an exchange or company, control access to the funds. Both the freedom and the responsibility are entirely yours\\n\\n---","blueprints":[],"quiz":[{"id":"q-base-g1-1","prompt":"What is the safest way to store the seed phrase when creating an OKX wallet (Step 3 of the guide)?","options":[{"id":"base-g1-1-1","label":"Take a screenshot and send it to yourself in Telegram Saved Messages","isCorrect":false,"feedback":"Incorrect. Write the words in order on paper and keep them somewhere secure, without saving them in the cloud or phone notes"},{"id":"base-g1-1-2","label":"Write the words in order on paper and keep them somewhere secure, without saving them in the cloud or phone notes","isCorrect":true,"feedback":"Correct. Write the words in order on paper and keep them somewhere secure, without saving them in the cloud or phone notes"},{"id":"base-g1-1-3","label":"Save it in a text file on the computer\'s desktop","isCorrect":false,"feedback":"Incorrect. Write the words in order on paper and keep them somewhere secure, without saving them in the cloud or phone notes"}],"explanation":"Write the words in order on paper and keep them somewhere secure, without saving them in the cloud or phone notes","sourceRef":"CAPITAL_BASE:2758–2774"},{"id":"q-base-g1-2","prompt":"Why should you check the new wallet address using DeBank in Step 7 of the guide?","options":[{"id":"base-g1-2-1","label":"To make sure the address exists and its balances are displayed correctly across all supported networks from an external view","isCorrect":true,"feedback":"Correct. To make sure the address exists and its balances are displayed correctly across all supported networks from an external view"},{"id":"base-g1-2-2","label":"To enable automated trading","isCorrect":false,"feedback":"Incorrect. To make sure the address exists and its balances are displayed correctly across all supported networks from an external view"},{"id":"base-g1-2-3","label":"To give DeBank permission to sign transactions","isCorrect":false,"feedback":"Incorrect. To make sure the address exists and its balances are displayed correctly across all supported networks from an external view"}],"explanation":"To make sure the address exists and its balances are displayed correctly across all supported networks from an external view","sourceRef":"CAPITAL_BASE:2808–2822"},{"id":"q-base-g1-3","prompt":"What should you do if the phone containing the wallet app is lost but the paper seed phrase is safe?","options":[{"id":"base-g1-3-1","label":"Ask a bank to reissue the blockchain account","isCorrect":false,"feedback":"Incorrect. Install the official app on a new device and import the wallet using the saved seed phrase"},{"id":"base-g1-3-2","label":"Install the official app on a new device and import the wallet using the saved seed phrase","isCorrect":true,"feedback":"Correct. Install the official app on a new device and import the wallet using the saved seed phrase"},{"id":"base-g1-3-3","label":"Consider the funds permanently locked","isCorrect":false,"feedback":"Incorrect. Install the official app on a new device and import the wallet using the saved seed phrase"}],"explanation":"Install the official app on a new device and import the wallet using the saved seed phrase","sourceRef":"CAPITAL_BASE:2823–2833"}],"source":{"file":"00_FREE_GIFT_MakeCash_Crypto_And_Capital_Base_15_Lessons.md","sha256":"88a3efb162434bb8a9b3b000caee579d9c27005a8ea46ddf4ef9cafb50dc45cc","lineStart":2718,"lineEnd":2858}}')}}]);